meta {
  name: Mail
  type: http
  seq: 6
}

post {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/mail
  body: json
  auth: none
}

body:json {
  {
    "recipient": "{{playerName}}",
    "subject": "GM API test",
    "text": "Hello from the Bruno collection.",
    "money": 1000
  }
}

docs {
  ## Mail

  Send a GM-stationery mail with text, optional money, and up to 12 item attachments.

  - Method and path: `POST /api/v1/mail`.
  - Body:
    - `recipient` is a character name; the character may be offline.
    - `subject` is at most 64 characters; `text` is at most 5000.
    - `money` is optional copper, at most 2147483646.
    - `items` is an optional array of `{"itemId": n, "count": n}`; after stack splitting the mail
      may carry at most 12 attachments.
  - Write gate: `GmApi.AllowWrites = 1`.
  - Permissions: `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_SEND_MAIL` (485) always, plus
    `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_SEND_ITEMS` (484) when items are attached and
    `RBAC_PERM_COMMAND_SEND_MONEY` (487) when money is sent.
  - Actor: signed `X-GM-Actor` game account id; must have security above `SEC_PLAYER`.
  - Target: the recipient account must be below the actor's security and not the actor's own
    account.
  - Success: `200` with `{"status":"ok"}`. Audit rows: `pending` then `success`.
  - Failure: `400 bad_request`, `invalid_item`, or `too_many_items`; `404 target_not_found`;
    `409 cannot_target_self` or `mailbox_full`; `500 mail_failed` or `audit_failed`.

  Mail bodies are not stored in the audit arguments.
}
